// @test: run-interpreter
// @level: L0
// @tier: 0
// @tags: verification, termination, total, soundness, ast-walk
// @expected-stdout: 0 6 6 0 ok
//
// Pin (T0786, SOUNDNESS) — the totality checker must see a recursive call
// wherever it is written.
//
// Both walks in termination.rs ended in a `_ => {}` annotated "other
// expressions we don't need to traverse for termination checking". They
// did need to: a call inside a tuple or a format-string interpolation was
// invisible, so
//
//     @total fn loops(n: Int) -> Int { (loops(n), 0).0 }
//     @total fn loops(n: Int) -> Int { f"{loops(n)}".len() }
//
// were ACCEPTED — `@total` granted to a function that does not terminate
// — while the direct, record-literal and array-literal spellings were
// correctly rejected with E321.  A totality claim that can be obtained by
// choosing where to write the call is worth nothing.
//
// This pin approaches it from the side a spec test can assert: every
// function below recurses through one of the once-invisible positions AND
// decreases, so each must be ACCEPTED and produce the right answer.  If a
// walk stops descending into one of these positions the call vanishes
// from the measure analysis; if it descends but mis-analyses it, the file
// is rejected.  Both failures are visible here, in opposite directions.
//
// A fourth position, an array literal, was drafted and dropped.  Written
// as `[via_array(n - 1)][0]` the file does not compile: the element type
// comes out as `!`, because the recursive callee's return type is not yet
// known while the literal is inferred.  `[2][0]` on a non-recursive
// element is fine, so this is narrower than "array literals" — it is
// self-reference inside a literal.  Left out rather than papered over, so
// this file states only what it can state honestly.  (That diagnostic
// also arrives with no source location.)
//
// The negative direction — unbounded recursion in the same positions
// being rejected — cannot be written as a run-interpreter spec (the file
// must compile to run), and is covered by the E321 measurements recorded
// in T0786.

@total
fn plain(n: Int) -> Int {
    if n <= 0 { return 0; }
    plain(n - 1) + n
}

@total
fn via_tuple(n: Int) -> Int {
    if n <= 0 { return 0; }
    (via_tuple(n - 1), 0).0 + n
}

@total
fn via_format(n: Int) -> Int {
    if n <= 0 { return 0; }
    f"{via_format(n - 1)}".len() + n
}

fn main() {
    print(f"{plain(0)} {plain(3)} {via_tuple(3)} {via_format(0)} ok");
}
